{
  "id": "python_py_fastapi_path_query",
  "title": "Path and query parameters",
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "testId": "python_test_py_fastapi_path_query_en",
  "estimatedMinutes": 17,
  "sources": [
    "https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/path-params/",
    "https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/query-params/"
  ],
  "spans": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "WHY USE THIS?\n",
      "size": 20,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "FastAPI builds JSON APIs that web and mobile applications call over HTTP; type annotations help validate inputs and describe the API contract.\n\n",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "PURPOSE AND REAL-WORLD USE\n",
      "size": 20,
      "color": "#6A1B9A",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "A path parameter identifies a resource; a query parameter controls filtering or paging. FastAPI derives parameter names and types from the Python function. Required and default values define the URL contract.\n\n",
      "size": 17,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "To run these examples locally, install ",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "pip install fastapi uvicorn httpx",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " plus any extra package named in the lesson. Save the server example as ",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "app.py",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " and start ",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "uvicorn app:app --reload",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": ". ",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "--reload",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " is for development only.\n\n",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "WHERE DOES THIS APPEAR IN REAL LIFE?\n",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "/books/12?limit=5",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " identifies book 12 and limits the list response to five items.\n\n",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "If this part is omitted: Without the path value the resource is unknown; removing the query value returns the endpoint to its default, unfiltered behavior.\n\n",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "COMPLETE RUNNABLE EXAMPLE\n",
      "size": 20,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "QUESTION: What will this code print? Predict first, then run it.\n",
      "size": 16,
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "from fastapi import FastAPI, Query\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\n@app.get(\"/books/{book_id}\")\nasync def read_book(book_id: int, limit: int = Query(default=10, ge=1, le=50)):\n    return {\"book_id\": book_id, \"limit\": limit}\n",
      "showCopyButton": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "REQUEST AND EXPECTED RESPONSE\n",
      "size": 18,
      "color": "#2E7D32",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "Request: GET /books/12?limit=5\nResponse: 200 OK; JSON: {\"book_id\":12,\"limit\":5}",
      "showCopyButton": false
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "LINE-BY-LINE CODE EXPLANATION\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "from fastapi import FastAPI, Query",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Imports a required type or tool; without it, the name is unavailable.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "app = FastAPI()",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — ",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "FastAPI()",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " creates the ASGI application that holds the routes and is passed to the server.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "@app.get(\"/books/{book_id}\")",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Binds an HTTP method and URL path to this function; without the decorator, it is not an API endpoint.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "async def read_book(book_id: int, limit: int = Query(default=10, ge=1, le=50)):",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Defines the endpoint the server calls; parameter names help bind path, query, or body data.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "return {\"book_id\": book_id, \"limit\": limit}",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Returns the HTTP response value; FastAPI converts it to JSON and applies the response model.\n\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "PRACTICE: CHECK IT WITH AN HTTP CLIENT\n",
      "size": 19,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "This complete file calls the app locally with TestClient; it does not open a server port. Install ",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "httpx",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " for TestClient.\n\n",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "COMPLETE RUNNABLE CLIENT TEST\n",
      "size": 20,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "QUESTION: What will this code print? Predict first, then run it.\n",
      "size": 16,
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "from fastapi import FastAPI, Query\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\n@app.get(\"/books/{book_id}\")\nasync def read_book(book_id: int, limit: int = Query(default=10, ge=1, le=50)):\n    return {\"book_id\": book_id, \"limit\": limit}\n\nfrom fastapi.testclient import TestClient\n\nwith TestClient(app) as client:\n    response = client.get(\"/books/12?limit=5\")\n    print(response.json())\n",
      "showCopyButton": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "EXPECTED CLIENT-TEST OUTPUT\n",
      "size": 18,
      "color": "#2E7D32",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "{'book_id': 12, 'limit': 5}",
      "showCopyButton": false
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "LINE-BY-LINE CODE EXPLANATION\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "from fastapi import FastAPI, Query",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Imports a required type or tool; without it, the name is unavailable.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "app = FastAPI()",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — ",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "FastAPI()",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " creates the ASGI application that holds the routes and is passed to the server.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "@app.get(\"/books/{book_id}\")",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Binds an HTTP method and URL path to this function; without the decorator, it is not an API endpoint.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "async def read_book(book_id: int, limit: int = Query(default=10, ge=1, le=50)):",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Defines the endpoint the server calls; parameter names help bind path, query, or body data.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "return {\"book_id\": book_id, \"limit\": limit}",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Returns the HTTP response value; FastAPI converts it to JSON and applies the response model.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "from fastapi.testclient import TestClient",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Imports TestClient so an HTTP request can exercise the app without opening a server port.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "with TestClient(app) as client:",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Creates a test HTTP client for the app and closes it when the context ends.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "response = client.get(\"/books/12?limit=5\")",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Sends the stated GET request through the test client and stores the response.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "print(response.json())",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Runs work for this request; its result or side effect affects the response.\n\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "COMMON MISTAKES\n",
      "size": 20,
      "color": "#C62828",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Putting a query value inside the path and leaving ",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "limit",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " unbounded; validate both URL shape and range.\n\n",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "tip",
      "title": "Practical tip",
      "text": "Try `/books/12?limit=5` in `/docs`; `book_id` is in the path and `limit` is in the query string after `?`."
    },
    {
      "type": "detail",
      "title": "One level deeper",
      "text": "The path carries resource identity; the query carries presentation or filter options. Use `Query(...)` to make a query parameter required."
    },
    {
      "type": "warning",
      "title": "Important warning",
      "text": "Do not concatenate user values into file paths or SQL; pass them as parameters and limit result counts."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "QUICK RECALL\n",
      "size": 20,
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Question: Which action best prevents the common mistake from this lesson?\n",
      "size": 16,
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Answer: Try ",
